# Line-ending policy.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on this machine, which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout.
# For most files that is harmless. For the program ledger it is not: ADR-0015
# documents an event record that was corrupted by a raw CR landing inside a JSON
# string value, and the pre-repair audit copies exist to preserve those exact
# bytes. A checkout that "helpfully" converts them destroys the evidence and
# invalidates the SHA-256 digests recorded in ADR-0015.
#
# -text disables all end-of-line conversion in both directions.

# Byte-for-byte evidence. Never convert, never diff as text.
.program/audits/malformed-events-pre-repair/** -text -diff

# Append-only event logs: LF in the repo, LF in the working tree.
.program/ledger/events/*.jsonl -text

# Hook denial log — same reason (written by tooling, read as evidence).
.program/audits/hook-denials.jsonl -text
